      "why": "iterative is the smallest-area family (single shared datapath, no pipeline registers, no k-way fanout). It is the only family I can plausibly use to hit min-area while still meeting >=1 MSPS if Fmax is high enough. I focus data_width 12-16 and n_iter 10-16 because the error constraint (<=2^-10) is the binding accuracy bound: too few iterations or too narrow a word fails it, and going much wider than ~16 wastes area for no accuracy gain (accuracy_bits ref is 10). angle_guard -2..1 and frac_guard 0..2 let the search trade a little accuracy headroom against area, and both rounding modes are kept since rounding can shave the error budget."
    }
  ,
